gunbc.rung_drop(
  id: value_position_prefix_not_operand_has_no_rust_operator_realization_row,
  rung: execution,
  statement: A prefix (one-operand) canonical operation in value-expression position has no Rust operator-realization row, so a prefix-not operand of a lowered conjunction cannot lower and the lowering refuses it with the named reason target_operator_realization_catalog_miss. This drop records that gap; the claims that would close it belong to v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position, which is the owner that re-enables the path by adding the target-language row. The lowering half of this row is NOT dropped: the plain two-operand Conj and Disj emission and its witness stage0_conjunction_emission_claims.dag are delivered here, and the row's done-condition stays that a prefix-free conjunction subject emits.,
  subject: The value-expression lowering path in module v2.std.compilers.target_model (the primitive-apply arms of target_project_body_arrow_expression_to_target_tokens and target_value_expression_primitive_apply_to_concrete_tokens, reached from target_project_body_expression_to_target_tokens) applied to a prefix canonical operation, and module v2.extdeps.languages.rust::rust_operator_realizations_catalog_node (the Rust operator-realization catalog). Concretely: a conjunction whose operand tree contains a prefix canonical operation (a not-node) reaching the primitive-apply path.,
  why_cannot_reach_rung: The target language defines no realization row for the one-operand operation, and the design forbids inventing one at the call site (a target-language-shaped emission requires a named realization in the target-language catalog, per v2.glossary::target_language_catalog). Measured at origin/main: v2.extdeps.languages.rust::rust_operator_realizations_catalog_node() authors exactly thirteen rows, each an InfixToken (or, and, ==, !=, <, <=, >, >=, +, -, *, /, <-); grep -in complement over module v2.extdeps.languages.rust yields 8 hits and none names a prefix token kind, an op_not row, or a bang token (the token module v2.extdeps.languages.rust::rust_token_bang() does not exist). The canonical operation itself exists: v2.std.compilers.target_model::canonical_operation_op_not(). The TypeScript target grounds op_not as a wire round-trip: module v2.test.claim.manual.target_operation_grounding_emit_typescript, the op_grounding_wire_roundtrips_all battery with its op_grounding_wire_roundtrips(operation: canonical_operation_op_not()) member; the Rust target has no such row. So on main a prefix-not operand reaches value-expression position with no nameable emission; after this row's lowering it refuses with the named reason target_operator_realization_catalog_miss, raised by v2.std.compilers.target_model::target_operator_realization_catalog_lookup (its lookup_otherwise tail) from v2.std.compilers.target_model::target_value_expression_primitive_apply_to_concrete_tokens. Measured: the reason-naming battery PASSes corpus_refusal_operator_realization_catalog_miss_holds and every other named-reason arm FAILs; the executed raw verdict lines are recorded durably at https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16957#issuecomment-7222732805 (log copy: ~/scratch/swift-hawk-617/logs/leg_NAMING.20261126T033521Z.log on HOST srv1 BOOT c095c0cd).,
  population: More than one authoring is affected by the missing target-language artifact rather than by one authoring's shape. Two measured instances: (1) a composite subject, a conjunction whose operand contains a prefix canonical operation - its refusal reason is target_operator_realization_catalog_miss (Run A in https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16957#issuecomment-7222732805: corpus_refusal_operator_realization_catalog_miss_holds PASSes and every other named-reason arm FAILs); (2) a standalone prefix subject (a prefix operation with a literal operand), which also refuses with target_operator_realization_catalog_miss and whose reason string is identical to instance (1)'s (Run B in the same comment: corpus_reason_equals_prefix_reason_holds PASSes). The population is therefore a missing target-language artifact, not one authoring.,
  restoration_trigger: Re-enable the path when the target-language catalog carries a row for the one-operand operation, named: module v2.extdeps.languages.rust::rust_operator_realizations_catalog_node gains a row whose canonical_operation equals v2.std.compilers.target_model::canonical_operation_op_not(), together with the operator-token and emitter-token that row names (the prefix token kind, which today does not exist in v2.extdeps.languages.rust - v2.extdeps.languages.rust::rust_token_bang() is absent), and the claims owned by v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position execute as PASS: prefix_not_emits_holds, prec_not_grouped_and_flat_bodies_differ_holds, prec_not_grouped_wraps_operand_holds (src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_conjunction_emission_claims.dag), conj_prefix_inner_emits_holds, disj_prefix_inner_emits_holds, negate_wrapped_operand_emits_holds (src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_conj_disj_prefix_inner_reason_probe.dag), and corpus_probes_emits_holds at v2.test.claim.self_host.stage0_production_corpus_probe.,
  displaced_cost: One corpus subject (src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_production_corpus_probe::corpus_probes_emits_holds, a prefix-not operand in value position) and six claims (prefix_not_emits_holds, prec_not_grouped_and_flat_bodies_differ_holds, prec_not_grouped_wraps_operand_holds in stage0_conjunction_emission_claims.dag; conj_prefix_inner_emits_holds, disj_prefix_inner_emits_holds, negate_wrapped_operand_emits_holds in stage0_conj_disj_prefix_inner_reason_probe.dag) remain refused, not emitted, until the prefix-not operator-realization row lands on v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position. No downstream consumer is broken by the refusal: the refusal is loud, typed and located (target_operator_realization_catalog_miss), which is what fail-closed demands.,
  created_at: 2026-11-26,
)
